 "brief": "# Build: skin-configuration-panel-before-ai-makes-a-skin-brett-picks-what-it-may-change\n\n## Brett said (verbatim)\n> \n\n## What to build\nContinue build \"Skin configuration panel: before AI makes a skin, Brett picks what it may change. The current look is saved as the Default skin. A full tree of options in categories (colors, typography, layout and tab placement, buttons and actions, behaviors, context menus with how deep to build them, nav menu, ap\" (skin-configuration-panel-before-ai-makes-a-skin-brett-picks-what-it-may-change) — Phase 2, model Opus.\nThis phase downgrades Fable → Opus: fine, no approval needed (it is recorded when you tick its first step).\nModel switches: a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. Fable upgrades need no approval right now (Brett, Nov 4 2026: \"If it needs Fable, set it to be Fable\"): a step that needs Fable (schemas, asset types, contracts, engines/kernel, cross-app protocols) is set to Fable and runs on Fable; the switch is recorded on the build. Never launch a step on a higher model than it is pinned to: raise the step first.\nRules: stay in this one session; no sub-agents; steps ≤ 30 min; read only the files listed; stop at the end of this phase.\nLook: UI code (handwritten or generated) conforms to the hot-swappable asset system: every colour, size, spacing, font, radius and border comes from asset tokens (--fx-* colour/style, --fx-type-* / --fx-dens-* / --fx-size-* scale, --fx-radius-*, --fx-border-w; Kotlin: Axf.colors / Axf.type / Axf.space / Axf.shapes), framework controls instead of raw ones, no var() fallbacks. `node framework/cli/check-theme.mjs` and `check-controls.mjs` must pass (CI fails otherwise); `node framework/cli/scale-adopt.mjs <path>` moves most literals onto the tokens.\nAPI: Everything comes with an API (Brett, Nov 8 2026): anything this build adds or changes that has a UI gets full API control: a deep link that opens it (console_show / console_open target), its state readable, and every action and setting it offers callable without the UI, through the console API (REST), MCP tools (console actions, plugin commands, control@1 for tokens and planner items), the CLI and voice (AmberX), all four the same. A UI-only feature is not done; say in the PR how each one is reached.\nBranch: claude/skin-configuration-panel-before-ai-makes-a-skin-brett-picks-what-it-may-change · PR #547\nSteps in this phase (6 left, ~2.7 h):\n[ ] s4 (~25 min) Make the AI skin maker obey the config: the generation brief carries only the allowed options and depth limits, and the output is validated against skin-config@1. Anything outside the allowed set is dropped and listed back to Brett.\n[ ] s5 (~25 min) Add the server side: theme-manager REST routes to read and save the skin config (GET/PUT skin-config, allow/lock one option, set depth, reset to default, save current look as Default) and to start an AI skin from a config. Store it per app on the hub.\n[ ] s6 (~25 min) Wire the API parity: CLI `skins.mjs config get|allow|lock|depth|reset|default|make`, MCP plugin commands from the routes, console actions skin.config.* for voice (AmberX), and the console_show deep link target `settings/appearance/skin-config`.\n[ ] s7 (~30 min) Build the Skin configuration panel in Settings → Appearance (shared AppearancePanel): a collapsible categorized tree from the engine with allow/lock switches per option and category, depth steppers for context and nav menus, a 'Default skin' row, and a 'Make skin with AI' button. Use TabGroup and framework controls only, tokens only, and the settings level toolbar.\n[ ] s8 (~25 min) Ship 3 UI Review options for the panel as settings assets (tree with switches, two-column picker, compact chip grid), then rebake the console, axHub web and AmberX shared assets.\n[ ] s9 (~30 min) Tests: engine fixtures, route tests, CLI tests, check-theme, check-controls, check-chrome-assets, check-skin-coverage, glossary catalog --check. Submit the desktop and phone screenshots of the 3 options to UI Review with --choices. Write _claude/builds/reports/skin-configuration-panel-before-ai-makes-a-skin-brett-picks-what-it-may-change.md, add a THREADS row, and open the PR. The PR says how each feature is reached (deep link, REST, MCP, CLI, voice).\nRead first: apps/console-web/plugins/theme-manager/, framework/core/engines/skin-config-rules.mjs, apps/console-web/plugins/theme-manager/server/, apps/console-web/plugins/theme-manager/plugin.json, framework/cli/skins.mjs, apps/console-web/plugins/theme-manager/commands.json, apps/console-web/src/actions/, apps/console-web/plugins/follow-amber/targets.json, framework/libs/settings/AppearancePanel.tsx, framework/libs/settings/SkinConfigPanel.tsx, framework/libs/settings/settings-assets/, apps/console-web/plugins/theme-manager/assets/settings/, framework/cli/shared-assets.mjs, apps/console-web/src/axf/, framework/spec/, apps/console-web/plugins/theme-manager/test/, _claude/builds/reports/skin-configuration-panel-before-ai-makes-a-skin-brett-picks-what-it-may-change.md, _claude/THREADS.md\nTick each step: node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs act step skin-configuration-panel-before-ai-makes-a-skin-brett-picks-what-it-may-change <stepId> done — it reaches main at once (builds-live). Link your branch / PR: node framework/cli/builds-live.mjs link skin-configuration-panel-before-ai-makes-a-skin-brett-picks-what-it-may-change --branch <b> --pr <n>.\nWatch live: when you start on a screen, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"…\"` so the live preview follows you.\nScreenshots that are not for approval (checking a screen, live captures, before/after): axf shot <file> --name \"…\" --app … --screen … --group \"<build name>\" (UI Review → Screenshots; ui-review-item@1), never the review queue.\n\n## Pipeline\nThis session was started by the orchestrator's dispatcher on Claude account mossesx-max- for the Opus phase. Tick every step as you finish it (orchestrator.mjs act step skin-configuration-panel-before-ai-makes-a-skin-brett-picks-what-it-may-change <stepId> done). When this phase's steps are done, stop: the dispatcher starts the next phase on the right account. If you must stop early with steps left, say why in a build note (orchestrator.mjs act note skin-configuration-panel-before-ai-makes-a-skin-brett-picks-what-it-may-change \"…\"); the build goes back to Pending for Brett.\n",
